BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Election Day Bike Bus
DTSTART:20261026T120000Z
DTEND:20261027T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261025T100655Z
UID:3db8cc78-d2e0-5c04-9734-9f8472e36c79
DESCRIPTION:The protected bike lanes along Bloor Street West between Islin
 gton and Royal York are gone.\n\nCycle Toronto will be leading a complimen
 tary bike bus shuttle on Election Day Monday\, October 26 through this new
  gap in our cycling network. All ages and abilities welcome. Together the 
 bike bus will safely ride and take the lane\, following all HTA regulation
 s. (Note: the protected bike lanes will remain intact east of Royal York a
 nd west of Green Lane until further notice.)\n\nThis destruction of life-s
 aving infrastructure is just the first step of the Ford government's $48M 
 scheme that won't solve traffic congestion and will put people's lives at 
 risk. While we continue the fight defend the rest of the 18 km targeted fo
 r removals in 2027\, we want to ensure folks in Etobicoke-Lakeshore can sa
 fely bike to the polls on Monday.\n\nLook for the Cycle Toronto flag and c
 argo bike!\n\nSee schedule below:\n\nDepartures Westbound Eastbound Royal 
 York & Bloor\n\nGreen Lane & Bloor\n\nnorth-east corner\n\nsouth-east corn
 er\n\n8:00 AM 8:15 AM 8:30 AM 8:45 AM 9:00 AM 9:15 AM 9:30 AM 9:45 AM 10:0
 0 AM 10:15 AM 10:30 AM 10:45 AM 11:00 AM 11:15 AM 11:30 AM 11:45 AM Break 
